{"title":"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Step_1:_using_the_symmetry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 1: using the symmetry</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Step_2:_multiplying_three_quadratic_terms\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 2: multiplying three quadratic terms</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Step_3:_Finding_a_root_of_q\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 3: Finding a root of q</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Step_4:_Partially_dividing_p\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 4: Partially dividing p</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Step_5:_Handling_the_remaining_part_of_p\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 5: Handling the remaining part of p</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Step_6:_Summary\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 6: Summary</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of the <i>real</i> roots of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6cc8e537ce4348c65cf554e04d6942516dd0b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^6+145x^4-2007x^3+145x^2+1=0.\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_1:_using_the_symmetry\">Step 1: using the symmetry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Step 1: using the symmetry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a34e0d2d21701d6bccfbe26fa1f954eb9dcd5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=x^6+145x^4-2007x^3+145x^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"318\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>The polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is symmetric. Each symmetric polynomial has the following property: for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5141b3b0adedf8965c49060e697689e88f77f6b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\not=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a root if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/5006cd2b2c3f4a71dbb3086ede030b29b4de6497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" /> is.\n</p><p>To see why this is true, assume that we have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5141b3b0adedf8965c49060e697689e88f77f6b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\not=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62bb264e9a12183ae79af158a7c97d6a52f1def3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=x^6+145x^4-2007x^3+145x^2+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"352\" height=\"19\" />. We can now divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed16c38e36fed49e600678cdfec693e8f45ff88e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^6$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. We get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b501eb82cd9560a9aff1d074e537ede5163bfd51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + \\frac{145}{x^2} - \\frac{2007}{x^3} + \\frac{145}{x^4} + \\frac{1}{x^6} = 0\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>But the left hand side is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab219f9cb516668d59da0ba90165b8a3eeed98e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\left(\\frac 1x\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"55\" height=\"45\" />. Thus also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8acae784f1dace3cd1ba505656911107e9210366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\left(\\frac 1x\\right)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"86\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_2:_multiplying_three_quadratic_terms\">Step 2: multiplying three quadratic terms</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Step 2: multiplying three quadratic terms\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Our polynomial has six complex roots: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd2ab862d8be4c90cbb73c59c931128b6cfe074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb87e7f3b2c3f25712d7563c74f262a3ebd3c413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476e7aaf00964af40209cca19590b10d2aa28155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />. It can be expressed as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9b6016ac39dfc8c7d6500ccd174842b6dd253d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p(x) = (x-\\alpha)(x-1/\\alpha)(x-\\beta)(x-1/\\beta)(x-\\gamma)(x-1/\\gamma)\\]\" width=\"459\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568fd41c394c1ca7ad90493c6a5ebbda3e5c9b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\alpha+1/\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/974370b3200d3633b856efef047a0f4d662dc369.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\beta+1/\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/973264bcefc92eff3d8e335e40abdb69b8e41f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\gamma+1/\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. We can then write:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41b49ed13e49bc7c902ccd11460b91e64f4d16f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p(x) = (x^2 - ax + 1)(x^2 - bx + 1)(x^2 - cx + 1)\\]\" width=\"370\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We can now compare the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> in this expression. (Comparing other coefficients is not necessary due to symmetry.) We get the following equations:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f72500d166e79a33eef5a7607210a4fd3f830d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a-b-c=0$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5e6e64e3ac710a92b78146ec70c41a72524c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+ab+ac+bc=145$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c6535105ef60cc07b7768a1b2df0774d892598d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-abc-2a-2b-2c=-2007$\" width=\"233\" height=\"12\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Simplifying, we get:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4c3e85710cff4f69bfec2adaff5ea38111a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0a36999cc689e066bc839a88fa8c7dd5e0683d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+ac+bc=142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536329f6d0e4095b3660588f6ec139fb3c5e1869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=2007$\" width=\"85\" height=\"12\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s formulas\">Vieta's formulas</a>, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60caf32f8f22c534ff01d52fe73229948e239342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q(x)=x^3 - 0x^2 + 142x - 2007$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_3:_Finding_a_root_of_q\">Step 3: Finding a root of q</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Step 3: Finding a root of q\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is increasing for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31ca9603d80ae55dd7c00a684e703b9c4513de93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q(0)&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has exactly one positive root. We can easily find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fb27d07d90956b15f82bad21f47e743efd9e68a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q(9)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />. Thus WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792fa2135a12f746ee8d35f224cc514437dd03c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=9$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>(Note: \nRemembering that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4c3e85710cff4f69bfec2adaff5ea38111a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536329f6d0e4095b3660588f6ec139fb3c5e1869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=2007$\" width=\"85\" height=\"12\" />, we now have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97c0c1d80f951a0cfc1244f53969a16cf433fffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c=-a=-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81f6b78332fd0dcaceb2402b2a8c52aa8b2db6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bc=2007/9=223$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />. \nFrom the first equation, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b739208c5f80b965dee4006248813651702932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-9-b$\" width=\"85\" height=\"12\" />. Substituting into the second one, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/89259ab09f12bb502c881ad95bc82ba9c5a51761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(b+9)=-223$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />. This obviously has no real solution, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are not real. But we don't need this observation.)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_4:_Partially_dividing_p\">Step 4: Partially dividing p</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Step 4: Partially dividing p\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We now know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e072441a63e11c62e948131864e1143aeed68b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2-9x+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. We can partially divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b73cc78665a71a6b4b71893201bcd7d0b3a50e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p(x) = (x^2 - 9x + 1)(x^4 + 9x^3 + 225x^2 + 9x + 1)\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_5:_Handling_the_remaining_part_of_p\">Step 5: Handling the remaining part of p</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Step 5: Handling the remaining part of p\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19dad061b5eb2e026948817a542ca47cd7cfa95f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(x)=x^4 + 9x^3 + 225x^2 + 9x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"19\" /> has no real roots.\n</p><p>To prove this, one can for example write:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0d02717d8494ddf63a9526f9ac83c83e3f4f63a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r(x) = \\left(x^4 + 9x^3 + \\frac{81}{4}\\cdot x^2\\right) + \\left(\\frac{81}{4}\\cdot x^2 + 9x + 1\\right) + \\left(225-2\\cdot\\frac{81}{4}\\right) x^2\\]\" width=\"545\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1ffbbc45b034d0d99b662e896211d91e9dd4c3ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r(x) = x^2\\left(x+\\frac92\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{9x}2+1\\right)^2 + \\frac{369}2\\cdot x^2\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"46\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_6:_Summary\">Step 6: Summary</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Step 6: Summary\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We found that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f466f4d4d579ad2d9dd4e6fe4b8bb4c47e8dae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=(x^2 - 9x + 1)r(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> has no real roots. Thus all real roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are the two real roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/94342a13ee436e0f3ffd775f6e751aedfe968817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 9x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />, and their sum is obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374ad4e9adc96666cde62dd31911b54d38e83c56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<pre>  roots of p computed by Octave:\n  -4.48006 + 14.30270i\n  -4.48006 - 14.30270i\n   8.88748 +  0.00000i\n   0.11252 +  0.00000i\n  -0.01994 +  0.06367i\n  -0.01994 -  0.06367i\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST\">2007 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARM